  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v9.3.2 - Discovery (9.x legacy line):\n\nOne fix: players are now reliably discoverable by servers. No API changes.\n\n- The mDNS advertiser announces its presence instead of only answering\n  queries. Advertising registered the records with a passive query responder\n  and multicast nothing, while a server's mDNS browser stops broadcasting\n  the service type once its startup queries are done - so a player that\n  started after the server was never discovered at all, and discovery only\n  appeared to work when the player was already running when the server came\n  up. The advertiser now multicasts its records unsolicited (RFC 6762\n  section 8.3) when advertising starts, and again whenever a network\n  interface appears - resume from sleep, a late-associating Wi-Fi - since\n  the announcement sent before that interface existed never reached it. The\n  announcement carries the full PTR/SRV/TXT/A set, so a server can connect\n  from its cache alone.\n\nNote: staying visible past the records' TTL still requires the player to\nhear the server's refresh queries, so allow inbound UDP 5353 through any\nhost firewall.\n\n----\n\n      Earlier release notes: https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet/releases",
